# Whitelist: ignore everything, then re-allow only the public dashboard files.
# Everything else in this folder (task SKILL.md files, sync machinery, logs)
# stays local-only and can never be committed to this public repo.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/claude.html
# theme.css: the shared palette, copied from the private theme pack. A named
# public file, the same pattern tests.html and make_favicon.py follow — NOT a
# loosening of the /* rule above. claude.html links it, so it must ship.
!/theme.css
!/tests.html
# index.html: what /artifacts/ serves. Without it GitHub Pages rendered
# README.md through Jekyll and served THAT as the index — no CSP, and a script
# from cdnjs, on the origin every app shares. Another named public file, same
# pattern as the ones above, not a loosening of /*.
!/index.html
# .nojekyll: an empty file whose presence turns off the Jekyll pass entirely, so
# no markdown in this repo can ever be published as a page again. Named for the
# same reason as everything else here — it must ship, and nothing else may.
!/.nojekyll
# privacy.html: the dashboard's privacy policy, linked from its footer. Another
# named public file, same pattern as the ones above — not a loosening of /*.
!/privacy.html
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
# NOTICE: the authorship/provenance statement that sits beside LICENSE. Another
# named public file, same as the ones above — not a loosening of the /* rule.
!/NOTICE
!/favicon.ico
!/make_favicon.py
# The workflows. Named file by named file, like everything above: the directory
# is re-allowed, then re-emptied, then each workflow is named. A new workflow
# needs its own line here or it silently won't be committed — which is how
# tests.html sat here for weeks with nothing running it.
!/.github/
/.github/*
!/.github/workflows/
/.github/workflows/*
!/.github/workflows/tests.yml
!/.github/workflows/codeql.yml
!/data/
/data/*
!/data/data-*.js
